How to build and run the OpenVX conformance tests on Android
============================================================

The conformance tests are built with CMake (see the top-level CMakeLists.txt).
On Android the same CMake project is cross-compiled using the CMake toolchain
file shipped with the Android NDK. The legacy ndk-build / Android.mk flow has
been removed because it did not enable the conformance feature-set macros and
did not build the NN "Networks" sources or the loadable test module, so it
produced an incomplete test binary.

Prerequisites
-------------
- Android NDK (r19 or newer; it bundles CMake and the toolchain file).
- CMake 3.10 or newer on the host.
- adb installed and configured (device connected / emulator running).
- An Android build of the OpenVX implementation under test, providing:
    * an 'include' directory with the OpenVX headers, and
    * a 'lib' directory with the implementation binaries
      (libopenvx.so and libvxu.so), built for the same ABI you target below.


1. Set the environment
-----------------------
    # Path to the Android NDK
    export ANDROID_NDK=<path to android-ndk>

    # Path to the OpenVX implementation package built for Android
    export OPENVX_DIR=<path to tested OpenVX implementation package>

    # Target ABI. Must match the ABI of the OpenVX implementation binaries.
    # Recommended for modern devices: arm64-v8a
    # Other valid values: armeabi-v7a, x86_64, x86
    export ANDROID_ABI=arm64-v8a

    # Minimum Android API level (adjust to match your device / OpenVX build)
    export ANDROID_PLATFORM=android-24


2. Configure and build
----------------------
    cd conformance_tests
    mkdir -p build-android && cd build-android

    cmake .. \
        -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${ANDROID_NDK}/build/cmake/android.toolchain.cmake \
        -DANDROID_ABI=${ANDROID_ABI} \
        -DANDROID_PLATFORM=${ANDROID_PLATFORM} \
        -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DOPENVX_INCLUDES=${OPENVX_DIR}/include \
        -DOPENVX_LIBRARIES="${OPENVX_DIR}/lib/libopenvx.so;${OPENVX_DIR}/lib/libvxu.so"

    cmake --build . -j

Notes:
  * The feature sets (Vision, Enhanced Vision, Neural Networks, Import/Export,
    U1, ...) are enabled by default. Toggle them with the same options used on
    other platforms, e.g. -DOPENVX_USE_PIPELINING=ON, -DOPENVX_USE_U1=OFF, etc.
  * NNEF import is enabled by default and needs the NNEF parser headers/libs.
    If they are not available for your Android build, disable it with
    -DOPENVX_CONFORMANCE_NNEF_IMPORT=OFF.
  * If the implementation needs extra link dependencies, append them to
    OPENVX_LIBRARIES (semicolon-separated), for example:
    "...;libopenvx.so;libvxu.so;log" .

After a successful build:
  * the test executable is at   build-android/bin/vx_test_conformance
  * loadable test modules are at build-android/lib/*.so


3. Deploy on the device and run
-------------------------------
Use the commands below as a sample; adjust paths to match your setup.

    DEVDIR=/data/local/tmp/openvx

    # Create the layout on device
    adb shell mkdir -p ${DEVDIR}/lib ${DEVDIR}/test_data

    # Upload the test executable
    adb push bin/vx_test_conformance ${DEVDIR}/
    adb shell chmod 755 ${DEVDIR}/vx_test_conformance

    # Upload loadable test module(s) built alongside the executable
    adb push lib/. ${DEVDIR}/lib/

    # Upload the OpenVX implementation shared libraries
    #   (refer to the OpenVX implementation documentation)
    (cd ${OPENVX_DIR}/lib; find . -name '*.so' -exec adb push {} ${DEVDIR}/lib/ \;)

    # Upload test data
    (cd ../../test_data; adb push . ${DEVDIR}/test_data/)

    # Run the tests on device
    adb shell "export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${DEVDIR}/lib:\${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}; \
               export VX_TEST_DATA_PATH=${DEVDIR}/test_data/; \
               ${DEVDIR}/vx_test_conformance"
